---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
---

<Layout>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Volt</h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        The AI coding agent that writes production-ready Structured Text. Compiles in your CODESYS, TwinCAT, or TIA Portal IDE.
      </p>
      <a href="#trial" class="cta">Start free trial</a>
    </section>

    <section class="features">
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>IDE-native</h3>
        <p>Bridges directly into your existing PLC IDE. No new editor. Your project state stays canonical in CODESYS / TwinCAT / TIA.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>IEC 61131-3 fluent</h3>
        <p>Fine-tuned on the actual ST language reference. Knows pragmas, FB lifecycle, init slots, shadowing — the silent quirks LLMs miss.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Spec → code</h3>
        <p>Upload a controls spec PDF. Volt generates function blocks that match your existing conventions and pass your compiler.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Autonomous fixes</h3>
        <p>Compiles, reads diagnostics, iterates. Surfaces the diff for you to approve. No silent overwrites.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>BYO AI client</h3>
        <p>Speaks MCP. Use Claude Code, Cursor, opencode — whatever you already pay for. Volt is the PLC-shaped backend.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Local-first bridge</h3>
        <p>The bridge daemon runs on the engineer's machine. No source code leaves your network without explicit push.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
